---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import pkg from '../../../package.json';
import bench from '../../../eval/benchmark-results.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Clueside | Local AI-image signals for your browser"
  description="Clueside surfaces local AI-image signals as you browse. Eligible images are analyzed inside Chrome. No image uploads, inference API, or backend."
>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Clueside home">
      <img src="/assets/mark.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32">
      <span>clueside</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a href="#how">How it works</a>
      <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a>
      <a href="#privacy">Privacy</a>
    </nav>
    <a class="button button-small button-ink" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside/releases/latest">Get the extension</a>
  </header>

  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero" id="top">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="live-dot"></span> Open source · MIT · Manifest V3</p>
        <h1>The clues stay<br>on <em>your side.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Clueside surfaces likely AI-generated images while you browse. The models run inside Chrome. Your images do not go anywhere.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-signal" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside/releases/latest">Download latest release</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside">Inspect the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <small class="release-note">The current v{pkg.version} release ships fully as Clueside, with both model weights bundled in the zip.</small>
        </div>
        <ul class="proof-list" aria-label="Key properties">
          <li><strong>0</strong> image uploads</li>
          <li><strong>2</strong> local neural heads</li>
          <li><strong>65%</strong> raw decision threshold</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="demo-shell" role="region" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
        <div class="demo-topbar">
          <div class="traffic" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <p id="demo-title">Interactive scoring explainer</p>
          <span class="local-pill">ON DEVICE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="demo-grid">
          <div class="sample-panel">
            <div class="sample-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Choose an illustrative sample">
              <button type="button" data-sample="real" aria-pressed="false">Real</button>
              <button type="button" data-sample="generated" aria-pressed="true">Generated</button>
              <button type="button" data-sample="uncertain" aria-pressed="false">Uncertain</button>
            </div>
            <div class="scan-frame photo-ai">
              <div class="landscape" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="sun"></span><span class="hill hill-a"></span><span class="hill hill-b"></span><span class="figure"></span>
              </div>
              <span class="scan-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="image-badge is-ai" data-badge>AI 91%</span>
            </div>
            <p class="demo-note">Illustrative scores. This demo does not analyze or upload an image.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="score-panel">
            <div class="score-readout">
              <span>fused p(AI)</span>
              <strong data-score>91%</strong>
              <small data-label>likely generated</small>
            </div>
            <div class="signals" role="group" aria-label="Illustrative scoring signals">
              <div class="signal-row"><span>CommunityForensics</span><i data-cf style="--value:84%"></i></div>
              <div class="signal-row"><span>DINOv2 probe</span><i data-dino style="--value:91%"></i></div>
              <div class="signal-row"><span>Metadata</span><b data-meta>generator trace</b></div>
              <div class="signal-row fusion"><span>Raw fusion</span><i data-fusion style="--value:91%"></i></div>
            </div>
            <div class="threshold-line"><span>0</span><mark>AI threshold 65%</mark><span>100</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="marquee" aria-label="Product principles">
      <div>NO CLOUD INFERENCE <span>◆</span> NO IMAGE API <span>◆</span> NO LOCAL SERVER <span>◆</span> WEBGPU + WASM <span>◆</span> PUBLIC BUILD STEPS</div>
    </section>

    <section class="section process" id="how">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="kicker">01 / What happens to an image</p>
        <h2>The browser is the lab.</h2>
        <p>Clueside reads an image already displayed in your tab, runs complementary signals locally, then places a confidence badge beside it. The image bytes never cross an inference server because there is no inference server.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="pipeline" role="group" aria-label="Local analysis pipeline">
        <article>
          <span class="step">01</span>
          <div class="step-icon pixels" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <h3>Read</h3>
          <p>Eligible webpage images are decoded inside the extension runtime.</p>
        </article>
        <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <article>
          <span class="step">02</span>
          <div class="step-icon split" aria-hidden="true"><i>CF</i><i>D2</i></div>
          <h3>Examine</h3>
          <p>Two neural views and provenance metadata look for different kinds of evidence.</p>
        </article>
        <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <article>
          <span class="step">03</span>
          <div class="step-icon gauge" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
          <h3>Fuse</h3>
          <p>A conservative policy protects real photos from a noisy second opinion.</p>
        </article>
        <span class="connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <article>
          <span class="step">04</span>
          <div class="step-icon badge-stack" aria-hidden="true"><i>AI</i><i>OK</i><i>?</i></div>
          <h3>Mark</h3>
          <p>Each eligible, successfully analyzed image gets a raw confidence score and a plain signal.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section badge-language">
      <div class="badge-copy">
        <p class="kicker">02 / One glance, four honest states</p>
        <h2>A signal, not a verdict from heaven.</h2>
        <p>AI detection is probabilistic. Clueside shows the score, preserves uncertainty, and says when an image could not be read. No fake certainty.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="legend-board">
        <div><span class="big-badge ai">AI <b>87%</b></span><p>Likely generated at or above your threshold.</p></div>
        <div><span class="big-badge ok">OK <b>18%</b></span><p>Likely a real photo based on local signals.</p></div>
        <div><span class="big-badge maybe">? <b>57%</b></span><p>Evidence is mixed. Treat it as uncertain.</p></div>
        <div><span class="big-badge skip">skip</span><p>The image was too small, blocked, or unreadable.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section evidence" id="evidence">
      <header class="section-heading evidence-heading">
        <p class="kicker">03 / Public evidence</p>
        <h2>Measured in the open.<br>Caveated in public.</h2>
        <p>The shipped policy is measured on a public, reproducible {bench.bench.n}-image benchmark through the same byte-exact preprocessing the extension runs, plus a {bench.stress.n}-image stock and catalog stress set that guards real-photo false positives. A higher-scoring legacy raw-max policy is not shipped because its live false positives were unacceptable. None of these numbers are a claim about POIDH's private evaluation set.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="metric-ledger">
        <div class="metric-main">
          <span class="metric-label">Shipped balanced accuracy</span>
          <strong>{bench.bench.ba}<span>%</span></strong>
          <p>raw 0.65 · v{pkg.version} · harness verified</p>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Current policy</dt><dd>{bench.bench.ba}%</dd><dd class="metric-detail">TPR {bench.bench.tpr}% · TNR {bench.bench.tnr}% · raw 0.65</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Real-photo pass</dt><dd>{bench.bench.tnr}%</dd><dd class="metric-detail">{bench.bench.falsePositives} false positive in {bench.bench.real} reals</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Legacy raw max</dt><dd>{bench.legacyRawMax.ba}%</dd><dd class="metric-detail">Not shipped · public fixture</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Public samples</dt><dd>{bench.bench.n}</dd><dd class="metric-detail">{bench.bench.ai} AI · {bench.bench.real} real</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="source-strip">
        <span>AI sources</span><p>DALL-E 3 · Flux 1.1 · GPT-4o · Midjourney · Stable Diffusion-era</p>
        <span>Real sources</span><p>COCO · Flickr30k · ImageNet-style · CelebA · Food101</p>
      </div>
      <p class="honesty-note">Honesty update, 2026-08-16: our own live-site smoke test of v1.2.0 failed on CDN-processed professional photography, and we published the full findings, isolation experiments, and fix plan in the repo. The benchmark above stays reproducible as stated; the live gap is being closed in the open, and contributions of live counterexamples are welcome.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside#local-benchmark">Read the benchmark method <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside/blob/main/docs/live-smoke-2026-08-16.md">Read the live smoke findings <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="section privacy" id="privacy">
      <div class="privacy-boundary">
        <span class="boundary-label">YOUR BROWSER</span>
        <div class="boundary-core">
          <img src="/assets/mark.svg" alt="" width="56" height="56">
          <div><strong>Image pixels</strong><small>decoded locally</small></div>
          <span>+</span>
          <div><strong>Model weights</strong><small>bundled locally</small></div>
          <span>=</span>
          <div><strong>Confidence</strong><small>shown locally</small></div>
        </div>
        <div class="blocked-route" role="img" aria-label="No image data leaves the browser"><span></span><b>NO IMAGE DATA</b><i>✕</i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="privacy-copy">
        <p class="kicker">04 / Privacy by architecture</p>
        <h2>We cannot keep your images because we never receive them.</h2>
        <p>Inference runs in a Manifest V3 offscreen document using WebGPU when available and WebAssembly everywhere else. There is no account, API key, cloud model, or localhost helper.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Models bundled in the release</li>
          <li>Works after the network is disconnected</li>
          <li>Source and build steps are public</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside/blob/main/PRIVACY.md">Read the privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section install" id="install">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">05 / Install from source or release</p>
        <h2>Three minutes.<br>No account.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol>
        <li><span>1</span><div><strong>Download and extract</strong><p>Get the latest release zip from GitHub.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>2</span><div><strong>Open Chrome extensions</strong><p>Visit <code>chrome://extensions</code> and enable Developer mode.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>3</span><div><strong>Load unpacked</strong><p>Select the extracted folder, pin Clueside, and reload your tab.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="install-actions">
        <a class="button button-signal" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside/releases/latest">Download release</a>
        <a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside#install">Build it yourself</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta">
      <p class="kicker">Open infrastructure for a synthetic web</p>
      <h2>Look twice.<br>Upload nothing.</h2>
      <p>Clueside is an independent open-source project by Luis Felipe Abarca, built for POIDH bounty 323.</p>
      <div>
        <a class="button button-ink" href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside">View on GitHub</a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://poidh.xyz/arbitrum/bounty/323">See the challenge <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <a class="brand" href="#top"><img src="/assets/mark.svg" alt="" width="28" height="28"><span>clueside</span></a>
    <p>Images never leave your device.</p>
    <div><a href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside">Source</a><a href="https://github.com/arcacomputer/clueside/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT License</a><span>© <span data-year></span> Luis Felipe Abarca</span></div>
  </footer>
  <script is:inline type="module" src="/app.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
